{"h": {"measure": "A", "k": 100, "noise": "N2"}, "sp": "nb", "rep": 129, "hyps": [{"edit_edge": 3, "edit_op": "none", "cond_edge": 4, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "lower", "why": "With edge 4 absent, deleting edge 3 leaves edge 5 as the only path into the output (or none at all), so accuracy collapses (exps 4, 6)."}, {"edit_edge": 3, "edit_op": "none", "cond_edge": 0, "cond_op": "skip_connect", "direction": "higher", "why": "In parameter-free, skip-heavy cells, removing the direct input-to-output skip pushes signal through deeper paths and improves accuracy (exp 9), whereas in conv cells it hurts."}, {"edit_edge": 5, "edit_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "cond_edge": 0, "cond_op": "skip_connect", "direction": "higher", "why": "Adding a 3x3 conv helps most when the rest of the cell lacks convolutions, e.g. skip-based cells (exp 19)."}, {"edit_edge": 0, "edit_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "cond_edge": 1, "cond_op": "skip_connect", "direction": "higher", "why": "When the parallel edge 0->2 is a parameter-free skip, the cell has little learnable capacity, so a conv on edge 0 adds much more (exp 28)."}, {"edit_edge": 5, "edit_op": "none", "cond_edge": 4, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "lower", "why": "Removing edge 5 when edge 4 is already none leaves at most the edge 3 path into the output, sharply cutting capacity or disconnecting the cell (exps 63, 64)."}, {"edit_edge": 5, "edit_op": "none", "cond_edge": 5, "cond_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "direction": "lower", "why": "Deleting a 3x3 conv on the last edge loses learnable capacity, while deleting a skip or pool there is neutral or beneficial (exps 61-64 vs 65-67)."}, {"edit_edge": 3, "edit_op": "nor_conv_1x1", "cond_edge": 4, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "higher", "why": "When edge 4 is missing, a conv on edge 3 restores a needed path to the output and gives large gains (exps 75, 78)."}, {"edit_edge": 3, "edit_op": "nor_conv_1x1", "cond_edge": 3, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "higher", "why": "Filling an empty edge 3 adds a new path to the output, which helps far more than replacing an existing skip, pool or conv there (exps 71, 75-79 vs 72-74)."}, {"edit_edge": 4, "edit_op": "skip_connect", "cond_edge": 3, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "higher", "why": "Without the input-to-output skip on edge 3, a skip on edge 4 supplies the residual path the deep conv cell needs (exp 34)."}, {"edit_edge": 1, "edit_op": "skip_connect", "cond_edge": 3, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "higher", "why": "When edge 3 is none, a skip on edge 1 provides a shortcut from the input that is otherwise missing, giving large ImageNet16-120 gains (exps 57, 58)."}], "tok": 17896, "bad": 0, "probes": [[["nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "skip_connect", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3"], [3, "none"]], [["nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3"], [3, "none"]], [["nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "avg_pool_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3"], [3, "none"]], [["nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "skip_connect", "none", "none"], [3, "none"]], [["nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "skip_connect", "nor_conv_3x3", "none"], [3, "none"]], [["nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "skip_connect", "none", "nor_conv_3x3"], [3, "none"]], [["none", "nor_conv_3x3", "none", "skip_connect", "none", "nor_conv_3x3"], [3, "none"]], [["nor_conv_1x1", "nor_conv_1x1", "nor_conv_1x1", "skip_connect", "nor_conv_1x1", "nor_conv_1x1"], [3, "none"]], [["skip_connect", "skip_connect", "skip_connect", "skip_connect", "skip_connect", "skip_connect"], [3, "none"]], [["avg_pool_3x3", "avg_pool_3x3", "avg_pool_3x3", "skip_connect", "avg_pool_3x3", "avg_pool_3x3"], [3, "none"]], [["nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "skip_connect", "nor_conv_3x3", "none"], [5, "nor_conv_3x3"]], [["nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "skip_connect", "nor_conv_3x3", "skip_connect"], [5, "nor_conv_3x3"]], [["nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_con